{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01358",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.31,
      "end_seconds": 4.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Sorry I'm a little late, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.16,
      "end_seconds": 10.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.63,
      "end_seconds": 23.35,
      "duration_seconds": 10.72,
      "text": "Mainly an itchy patch on my wrist. There's a couple of other things, uh, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.39,
      "end_seconds": 29.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Alright, can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.1,
      "end_seconds": 34.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Let me think, ever since... since Friday, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.5,
      "end_seconds": 43.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.17,
      "end_seconds": 50.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "Moisturiser helps a bit. Mild, really. It's worse with my new watch strap."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.41,
      "end_seconds": 66.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.81,
      "end_seconds": 75.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.15,
      "text": "It's, It's sitagliptin, 100 milligrams, once a day for my sugar. I take a plain moisturiser, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.66,
      "end_seconds": 80.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.53,
      "end_seconds": 84.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "My daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.36,
      "end_seconds": 95.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.82,
      "end_seconds": 99.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.14,
      "end_seconds": 105.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Have you retired yet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.99,
      "end_seconds": 111.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.97,
      "end_seconds": 116.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.68,
      "end_seconds": 120.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.85,
      "end_seconds": 129.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.82,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.03,
      "end_seconds": 132.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "I've got diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.03,
      "end_seconds": 152.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Okay, did you get fever, spreading or blisters?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.27,
      "end_seconds": 158.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "I haven't had fever, spreading or blisters, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.11,
      "end_seconds": 165.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "So, any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.1,
      "end_seconds": 167.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.69,
      "end_seconds": 171.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.26,
      "end_seconds": 173.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.67,
      "end_seconds": 178.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.33,
      "end_seconds": 193.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.49,
      "end_seconds": 221.43,
      "duration_seconds": 10.94,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 16, SpO2 98 percent on room air, pulse 73. And temp 36.7 degrees, BP is 112 over 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.29,
      "end_seconds": 227.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.53,
      "end_seconds": 231.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Right, look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.6,
      "end_seconds": 254.61,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "There's a neat red patch where the watch strap sits, with a little scaling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.57,
      "end_seconds": 260.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Right, good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.42,
      "end_seconds": 286.57,
      "duration_seconds": 9.15,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is mild contact dermatitis from the watch strap."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.16,
      "end_seconds": 291.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.91,
      "end_seconds": 317.01,
      "duration_seconds": 25.1,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like mild contact dermatitis from the watch strap. I'd like you to take hydrocortisone cream, 1%, once a day, one week. That should help with contact dermatitis. Stop wearing that strap and keep the skin moisturised. Do get help quickly if it spreads or blisters. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.56,
      "end_seconds": 322.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.42,
      "end_seconds": 326.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}